# Terraform lifecycle convergence

Follow ADR-0025 and the lifecycle language in `CONTEXT.md`.

- Classify every managed resource and relationship exactly once as Durable or Recreatable.
- Place Durables in `module.durables` and Recreatables in conditional `module.recreatables`.
- A Durable may depend only on Durables. Converge the complete Durable module before the Recreatable module.
- Give every Durable `prevent_destroy`; only Teardown may lift it.
- Park must use a non-sticky intent and a complete Terraform plan. Do not use routine `-target`, State edits, or duplicated preserve lists.
- Give each remote fact one Terraform owner. Count implicit provider side effects as writers.
- Never mix an aggregate collection owner with resources that own members of that collection.
- On DigitalOcean, leave `digitalocean_project.resources` unset. Own disjoint memberships with `digitalocean_project_resources` in the member's lifecycle module.
- An Additive Stack Change must preserve every existing identity, desired attribute, and relationship throughout Apply.
- Apply and Park must be retry-convergent after supported partial failure; repeating the command must end in an empty plan.
- Pin provider versions exactly. Lifecycle, membership, and provider-version changes require the ADR-0025 live lifecycle matrix before merge.
- Fail closed on external drift and unmanaged collisions. Do not auto-adopt or add compatibility paths.
